  "notes": "つぐ has different meanings depending on the kanji used.\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION:\n- {次|つ}ぐ: to come next, to follow in rank\n- {継|つ}ぐ: to inherit, to succeed (position/business)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS WITH {次|つ}ぐ:\n- Xに{次|つ}ぐ: second to X, after X\n- {相|あい}{次|つ}ぐ: to happen one after another\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS WITH {継|つ}ぐ:\n- {家業|かぎょう}を{継|つ}ぐ: to take over family business\n- {伝統|でんとう}を{継|つ}ぐ: to carry on tradition\n- {後|あと}を{継|つ}ぐ: to succeed someone\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive with {次|つ}ぐ; transitive with {継|つ}ぐ.",
